  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "History of knot theory (Przytycki, arXiv:math/0703096, chapter of KNOTS) — from Gauss and Listing through Kelvin, Tait, Kirkman and Little to the twentieth century\n\n**KNOTS: From combinatorics of knot diagrams to combinatorial topology based on knots**, Chapter II *History of Knot Theory* — Józef H. Przytycki. arXiv:math/0703096v1 [math.GT] (2007).\n\nA survey chapter of the author's book project: early knot drawings, Gauss's linking integral, Listing, the vortex-atom programme of Thomson and Tait, the knot tables of Tait, Kirkman and Little, and the development into combinatorial topology and the Jones-polynomial era. Rich in primary quotations and a long bibliography (209 references extracted).\n\n**Why it may bear here.** Registered as `przytycki2007knothistory`; cited in the knotted-particles history for the abandonment of the vortex atom and the birth of knot tables. Six images are not yet described (ingested with the image-description step deferred).",
